# Rust / Cargo
target
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo.lock used to be ignored outright. Every workspace here produces a
# binary — the root one, and the seven standalone tools that declare their own
# `[workspace]` — so all eight lockfiles are committed. The one dependency that
# makes this load-bearing rather than tidy is `big_space`, taken from a git
# branch rather than a version: without a lockfile "the branch" resolves to
# whatever its head was that morning, under a four-platform determinism matrix
# whose entire claim is byte-identical output.
#
# Vendored crates are path dependencies of the root workspace and resolve
# through its lockfile; one of their own would only ever be a build artifact of
# someone testing them standalone.
vendor/*/Cargo.lock

# Editor / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store

# Logs / telemetry / test output
*.log
*.tmp
p2-kill9-*/
p2-abba-*/
p2-gateway-*/
p3-island-*/

# Agent worktrees. These are full checkouts with their own .git, so a stray
# `git add -A` stages three embedded repositories instead of ignoring them.
.claude/worktrees/

# Device-local agent state: memory, lanes and leases. Never committed.
# The real store is the git common directory (see scripts/agent-lane.sh);
# .agents/memory is a symlink into it, so every worktree sees one set of notes.
.agents/

# Local single-node FoundationDB dev cluster (slice 3 test harness).
# Never committed. See .fdb-dev/README.md.
.fdb-dev/
.omo
